According to this perspective, the South Korean government under President Syngman Rhee was determined to crush the North Korean communist regime and reunify the peninsula under its rule. The South Korean military launched a surprise attack across the 38th parallel in June 1950, aiming to capture Pyongyang and topple the North Korean government. However, the North Korean military responded quickly and effectively, pushing the South Korean forces back across the border.

From then on, the North Korean military took the initiative, driving the South Korean forces down to the southern tip of the peninsula. The US intervened in September 1950, but even then, the North Korean military continued to gain ground until they were finally halted at the 38th parallel in October 1950.

